Draugr      dev  (latest: vv9.9.9. Run 'draugr self-update')

TOOLS
Tool         Status      Version  Notes
cosign       – optional  -        optional: https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/system_config/installation/
git          ✗ missing   -        install: https://git-scm.com/downloads
gitleaks     ✗ missing   -        install: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks#installing
gosec        ✗ missing   -        install: https://github.com/securego/gosec#installation
govulncheck  ✗ missing   -        install: draugr tools install govulncheck, it is distributed as a Go package and needs a Go toolchain to build
grype        ✗ missing   -        install: https://github.com/anchore/grype#installation
kube-bench   ✗ missing   -        install: https://github.com/aquasecurity/kube-bench/releases, extract both the binary and its cfg/ directory
kubectl      ✗ missing   -        install: https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/
notation     ✗ missing   -        install: https://notaryproject.dev/docs/user-guides/installation/cli/
nuclei       ✗ missing   -        install: https://docs.projectdiscovery.io/tools/nuclei/install
retire       ✗ missing   -        install: npm install -g retire, retire.js publishes to npm only, so it needs a Node runtime
semgrep      ✗ missing   -        install: https://semgrep.dev/docs/getting-started/
syft         ✗ missing   -        install: https://github.com/anchore/syft#installation
trivy        ✗ missing   -        install: https://trivy.dev/latest/getting-started/installation/

NETWORK  (what Draugr fetches, and when · --offline stops all of it)
  draugr tools install             each tool's pinned release archive, verified against a recorded SHA-256
  draugr feeds update              the CISA KEV catalog and the FIRST EPSS scores
  draugr self-update               the latest draugr release
  draugr doctor                    the latest draugr release, to compare against yours (skipped by --offline)
  a scan, before it starts         the reference data each scanner reads, host by host under HOSTS
  a scan, per target               the registry, for an image; the endpoint itself, for a host or DAST target
  a scan, with the threats control abuse.ch, which learns each host's name

HOSTS  (a scan contacts these; for an egress allowlist)
  ghcr.io                   vulnerability database · before the scan
  github.com                template set · before the scan
  grype.anchore.io          vulnerability database · before the scan
  mirror.gcr.io             vulnerability database · before the scan
  raw.githubusercontent.com advisory database · before the scan
  semgrep.dev               rule pack · every scan
  tuf-repo-cdn.sigstore.dev Sigstore trust root · before the scan
  vuln.go.dev               vulnerability database · every scan

13 of these are not installed. Which you need depends on your descriptor. Run `draugr doctor <saga>` to check just those, or `draugr tools install` to fetch them all.
